    <version>1.5.1</version>
    <time>1787063839</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Reproducibility fix: move the hash-based bytecode recompilation and fdupes from %check to %install, so the package content no longer varies when built with --nocheck (boo#1227364). Same fix bmwiedemann applied to python-langgraph in sr#1371636.</comment>
    <requestid>1371666</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="11" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>ce27a7b3369cf0be43166bd0d4ac95a5</srcmd5>
    <version>1.6.0</version>
    <time>1787235326</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- Update to 1.6.0:
  * Map OpenAI SDK failures onto the new standard model exception
    types from langchain-core 1.6.0
  * Raise a clear error on an unexpected response type in
    _create_chat_result
- Follow upstream and raise the langchain-core requirement floor
  to 1.6.0

Also carries 1.5.2 (devel had it; Factory is 1.5.1):
- Update to 1.5.2:
  * Preserve consecutive reasoning-item boundaries when converting
    v1 content blocks back to Responses API input
  * Extract LangSmith gateway metadata from response headers
  * Support o-series models in get_num_tokens_from_messages
- Add python-httpx2 as a test BuildRequires
- Deselect the o-series token-counting unit test that would
  download a tiktoken BPE encoding in the offline build

INTERDEPENDENT REQUESTS - please stage together (will not build until these land):
 * python-langchain-core 1.6.0
 * python-langchain-openai 1.6.0 (also carries 1.5.2 vs Factory 1.5.1)
 * python-langchain-anthropic 1.6.0
Devel accepts: sr#1372135 (core), sr#1372136 (openai), sr#1372137 (anthropic).
</comment>
    <requestid>1372139</requestid>
  </revision>
